WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.200
Speaker 1: We are starting today with what
are effectively, in a sense, counter sanctions,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:12.049
sanctions issued not only sanctions but also
bans from the country of Russia issued by

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:16.840
the Kremlin against the number of American
officials up to and including Joe Biden.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:24.480
Now there's not very much that's funny about
what's going on with the Russian invasion

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.480
of Ukraine.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.619
There's just very little that's funny in all
of this.

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:33.460
But the sanctions and banning Biden from Russia,
it's a little bit funny.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:38.350
I will tell you, there's a Newsweek piece
about this Russia sanctions Joe and Hunter

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.239
Biden, which I just find hilarious.

00:00:41.239 --> 00:00:47.250
Hillary Clinton and 10 others President Joe
Biden, his son, Hunter Biden, Hillary Clinton

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.950
and 10 other officials have been sanctioned
by Russia in response to the sweeping sanctions

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:56.390
imposed by Washington, the Russian government
announced today yesterday.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:01.679
Rather, the sanctions barred the officials
from entering Russia.

00:01:01.679 --> 00:01:06.110
Russia's Foreign Ministry said in a statement
translated to English that the measures were

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:09.440
on the basis of reciprocity now here.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:16.290
It's actually beneficial that the people that
are sanctioned don't need to go to Russia

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:20.250
and don't have bank accounts in Russia and
don't have assets in Russia, and it makes

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.110
it all pretty weak.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:26.240
Now you'll remember that Russian oligarchs,
organizations and entities have been targeted

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:32.409
by U.S., Europe and Canada in response to
the Ukrainian invasion by Russia.

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:36.010
Russian President Putin himself has been directly
sanctioned.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:40.360
The translated Russian Foreign Ministry statement
Tuesday said the reciprocal sanctions were

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:47.840
the inevitable consequence of the extremely
Russo phobic Russia phobic course taken by

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.659
the administration.

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:52.010
Others sanctioned by Russia.

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.119
Secretary of State Antony Blinken.

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:58.409
Defense Secretary Lloyd Austin, chairman of
the Joint Chiefs Mark Milley.

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:00.740
CIA Director William Joseph Burns.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:05.100
White House Press Secretary Jen Psaki, even
Jen Psaki.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.300
And a bunch of other people now.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:14.060
Jen Psaki was asked about this yesterday,
and she basically made the obvious points

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.550
about it.

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:16.550
Take a listen to this.

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:21.020
Speaker 2: And one more of the sanctions were
imposed today by Russia against yourself,

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:23.720
President Biden and other top U.S. officials.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.190
Do you have a response to that?

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.820
And how will it impact any of you, if at all?

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:34.520
Sure, I would first note that President Biden
is a junior, so they may have sanctioned his

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.520
dad.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.520
May he rest in peace?

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:37.520
Speaker 1: Can you imagine?

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.620
I mean, this is one of those things where,
you know, in the United States what I love,

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:47.470
what Jen Psaki is saying, because it's almost
too on the nose.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:48.770
And also irrelevant.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:52.420
If you understand how Russia works, let me
explain what I mean by that.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:59.530
On the one hand, in the U.S., if you sanction,
you know, Joseph Biden rather than Joseph

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:03.570
Biden Jr., you've not sanctioned the correct
person.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.350
It doesn't matter what your intent was.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:09.920
In some places, there's other places where
intent does matter, but it's sort of like

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:10.920
a legal question.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.640
But we have the general belief in the U.S.
where like, that's a legit technicality, where

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.800
like if you don't say that it's junior, it
probably applies to someone other than the

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.780
person it's supposed to apply to.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.690
And Jen Psaki is right about that.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:27.540
But the other thing you have to understand
is in Russia, they don't care about technicalities

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.890
like that.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:33.640
If the intention was to sanction Joe Biden,
the president of the United States, the fact

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:38.240
that Joe Biden is Biden's dad, deceased father,
they don't.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.070
Those are not the types of technicalities
that courts in Russia care about unless it's

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:47.480
to their advantage, in which case all sorts
of technicalities you couldn't even imagine

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.480
will matter.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:52.140
There's a bunch of interesting books that
talk about this, including Bill Browder's

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.100
book I believe it's called Red Notice.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.120
He's been a guest on the show, even if you
don't like Bill Browder or you don't find

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.420
him trustworthy.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:04.900
His explanation of how the the justice system
is a very amorphous thing in Russia are quite

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.310
quite interesting.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.780
Let's get a little more here from Jen Psaki.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:13.140
Speaker 2: It's the second piece, I would
say, is that won't surprise any of you, that

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:16.280
none of us are planning tourist trips to Russia.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:21.079
None of us have bank accounts that we won't
be able to access, so we will forge ahead.

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:22.079
Yeah.

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:27.720
Speaker 1: At this point, I don't think anybody
is really looking to go to Russia from American

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.140
leadership.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:36.090
It's interesting that Hillary's on the list,
but no Trump sanction, no Trump ban.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.730
Also notable and interesting.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:44.130
And of course, this is serious fuel for the
conspiracy theorists.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:51.410
The conspiracy theorists are hearing this
and they are coming up with all sorts of different

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:55.750
hypotheses about why this is the list and
why is Hillary on the list?

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:59.760
That that's that's a really, really big deal.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.010
To them, anything else of interest here?

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:05.080
Um.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:10.180
Oh, this is notable at the same time, Russia
does not refuse to maintain official relations

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:14.830
if they meet our national interests, so they're
making it clear that even though these people

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:22.480
are banned and not allowed in Russia, if there
were some particular reason why they would

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:25.250
want to meet with people or maintain a diplomatic
relation, they will do that.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.070
Of course, that that makes perfect sense.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:29.000
Not a big surprise.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:34.020
Imagine if they included Hunter Biden's laptop
on the list.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.950
That would be pretty fascinating.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:52.490
That would be 

00:05:52.490 --> 00:06:31.760
pretty fascinating.

